{% extends "_layout.njk" %}
{% block content %}
    <div class="page-head">
      <div class="kicker">Connections</div>
      <h1>The web of connections</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">{{ site.uniqueConnections | num }} hand-made links across {{ site.readCount }} books. None of them were generated by similarity scoring.</p>
    </div>

    {# 5a — TEXT LAYER. Indexable, always present, and readable with JavaScript off.
       Everything below this comment renders server-side. #}
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Every book on this shelf carries a small set of explicit links to other books. There are {{ site.uniqueConnections | num }} of them. They are made by hand, one at a time, and each one means something specific &mdash; not &ldquo;these are both about finance,&rdquo; which is what a tag is for, but that one book is the prequel to another, or refutes it, or describes the same mechanism in a different domain.</p>
      <p>The links accumulate rather than being designed. A book arrives, it gets read, and the question is which of the {{ site.readCount }} books already on the shelf it argues with. Most books attach to five or six. A few attach to twenty. And some attach to almost nothing, which is its own kind of information &mdash; books that connect to nothing are, in my experience, disproportionately books that said nothing.</p>
      <p>About seventy-five of the pairs here point one way only. That is deliberate: a later book often comments on an earlier one that has nothing to say in return. Both pages show the link; only one of them claims it. There is more on the method in <a href="/reading">why I track the connections between books</a>.</p>
    </div>

    {# 5c/5d/5e — INTERACTIVE LAYER. Everything above works without it. #}
    <section class="pagesec">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Explore the map</h2></div>
      <div class="pathfinder">
        <label class="pf-field"><span>From</span><input id="pfA" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Start with a book&hellip;"><ul class="pf-list" id="pfListA"></ul></label>
        <label class="pf-field"><span>To</span><input id="pfB" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="&hellip;and end with another"><ul class="pf-list" id="pfListB"></ul></label>
        <button class="ctl-btn" id="pfGo">Find the chain</button>
      </div>
      <div class="pf-result" id="pfResult"></div>

      {# Focus mode (5c). Rendered by graph.js; on a phone this is the default view
         and the canvas is never built at all. #}
      <div class="ego" id="egoPanel"></div>

      <div class="graph-wrap">
        <div class="graph-tools">
          <input id="gsearch" class="gsearch" type="search" placeholder="Find a book in the web&hellip;" autocomplete="off">
          <button class="lreset" id="graphReset" type="button">Reshuffle &#8635;</button>
          <button class="lreset" id="egoBack" type="button" style="display:none">&larr; Whole map</button>
          <span class="ghint">Books cluster by theme. Hover to reveal threads &middot; click to open &middot; scroll to zoom</span>
        </div>
        <canvas id="graphCanvas"></canvas>
        <div class="glegend" id="graphLegend"></div>
        <div class="gnodecard" id="gcard"></div>
      </div>
      <p class="pagesec-intro" style="margin-top:14px">On a phone this opens in focus mode &mdash; one book, its connections, and theirs &mdash; which is readable where a {{ site.readCount }}-node graph is not. Tap any neighbour to travel to it.</p>
    </section>

{# 5b — THEME MATRIX. Ten nodes instead of {{ site.readCount }}. Computed at build
       time, rendered as a real table so it is legible on a phone and to a crawler. #}
    <section class="pagesec">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Where the shelf connects to itself</h2></div>
      <p class="pagesec-intro">Connection density between themes, counting every linked pair. The library has two dense clusters that barely touch each other, and one thin bridge from history into technology.</p>
      <div class="matrix-wrap">
        <table class="matrix">
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Number of connections between each pair of themes</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Theme</th>{% for t in themesCfg %}<th scope="col" abbr="{{ t.name }}"><span>{{ t.name }}</span></th>{% endfor %}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>
          {# Nunjucks has no `loop.parent` — that is Jinja2, and it silently evaluates to
             undefined, which is why every cell in this table used to render empty. Capture
             the row index in a variable before entering the inner loop. #}
          {% for t in themesCfg %}
            {% set row = loop.index0 %}
            <tr><th scope="row">{{ t.name }}</th>
            {% for u in themesCfg %}
              {% set n = matrix[row][loop.index0] %}
              <td{% if row == loop.index0 %} class="diag"{% endif %}{% if n and row != loop.index0 %} style="--heat:{{ n / matrixMax }}"{% endif %} data-n="{{ n }}">{% if n %}{{ n }}{% endif %}</td>
            {% endfor %}
            </tr>
          {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <ul class="matrix-top">
        {% for p in crossPairs | take(6) %}<li><strong>{{ p.n }}</strong> {{ p.a }} &harr; {{ p.b }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>

{# 5a — FEATURED PAIRS. Alex's hand-written pairs are §19 open item 3. Until those
       land these are the pairs with the strongest shared footing, computed at build time. #}
    <section class="pagesec">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Pairs worth reading together</h2><span class="sub">{{ featured.length }} pairs</span></div>
      {% if featuredProvisional %}<p class="pagesec-intro">Selected by the data &mdash; the pairs that share the most themes and tags. The hand-written notes on why each pair talks to each other are still to come.</p>{% endif %}
      <div class="pairlist">
        {% for p in featured %}
        <div class="pair">
          <a class="pair-side" href="{{ p.a.href }}"><span class="pair-t">{{ p.a.shortTitle }}</span><span class="pair-a">{{ p.a.author }}</span></a>
          <span class="pair-link" aria-hidden="true">&harr;</span>
          <a class="pair-side" href="{{ p.b.href }}"><span class="pair-t">{{ p.b.shortTitle }}</span><span class="pair-a">{{ p.b.author }}</span></a>
          <span class="pair-why">{{ p.sharedThemes | join(" &middot; ") | safe }}{% if p.sharedTags.length %} &mdash; both tagged {{ p.sharedTags | take(3) | join(", ") }}{% endif %}</span>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}<script src="/assets/js/graph.js" defer></script>{% endblock %}
